301
      Figure 3 shows the pattern in individual images. On a chest radiograph, the Effusion and Nodule
302
      writes raise the same answers. The competing write raises the Effusion answer more than the
303   Effusion write does. On a natural image, the dog write moves only the dog answer. The write
304   matrix reveals two components of the deficit (Figure 4, Table 10). First, concept writes have little
305   effect on their own answers in the chest datasets. The median 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 is 0.015 on NIH and 0.022 on
306   CheXpert, compared with 0.270 on COCO. Writes meet the steering reference—beating the random
307   family and the sham—in 44 of 234 chest cells, versus 102 of 114 COCO cells. Second, competing
308   directions share the effect when a chest write moves an answer. In 15 of those 44 cells, a competing
309   clinical direction moves the answer at least as much. Across the grid, the Atelectasis, Effusion, and
310   Consolidation directions raise each other’s answers by similar amounts. On COCO, the diagonal entry
311
      of 𝑊 dominates its row. On NIH and CheXpert, the row is flat or peaks off the diagonal. At every
      Qwen2.5-VL size, a competing direction—Cardiomegaly at 3B, Nodule at 7B and 32B, Atelectasis at
312
      72B—raises the Effusion answer more than the Effusion direction does.
313
314
315
      5.2     The seed finding replicates on new patients
316
      The evaluation builds on a two-model NIH study of Qwen2.5-VL-7B and LLaVA-1.5-7B (Appendix B).
317
      The central result reproduces in a 600-image cohort disjoint from every earlier cohort (Table 22).
318   The Effusion write raises the Effusion answer by 0.190. This increase exceeds the random 95th
319   percentile (0.137) and sham (0.017). It ranks second among the 120 compared effects. Yet the Nodule
320   direction raises the Effusion answer by 0.262. Effusion ownership is 𝑂 Effusion = −0.071 (95% CI
321   [−0.080, −0.062]), matching the original −0.057 [−0.069, −0.045]. Prompt dependence for Mass
322   also reproduces. Effusion and Cardiomegaly are the most readable chest concepts (mean selectivity
323   0.17 and 0.19 over 40 chest blocks). Effusion is owned in 6 of 39 chest blocks. Of these owned
      blocks, 5 have 𝑂 Effusion ≤ 0.03.


