354   5.3                                              The write mechanism is intact on natural objects
355
356
      The same procedure produces the opposite result on COCO (Table 1, right block). Objects are owned
      in 100 of 114 cells (88%), with ownership margins of 0.1–0.9 in the Qwen, Lingshu, and Gemma
357
      families. 102 cells meet the steering reference. Only 6 cells have a stronger competitor. Of the 19
358
      checkpoints with a COCO block, 17 own at least four of the six objects. Dose response tracks the write.
359   Across questions and blocks on COCO, median ownership rises from −0.03 at 𝛼 = −0.1 to +0.26
360   at 𝛼 = +0.25 and remains positive at 𝛼 = +0.5 (+0.18). On NIH, median ownership stays within
361   ±0.1 at every dose (Figure 2c). The write, direction construction, reference family, and decision rules
362   therefore work as intended. The deficit is specific to clinical concepts.
363
364   5.4                                              Ownership belongs to the reader
365
366   Gemma 3 shares one SigLIP tower across its 4B, 12B, and 27B checkpoints. MedGemma shares
367   one MedSigLIP tower across 4B and 27B. LLaVA-1.5 shares one CLIP tower across 7B and 13B.
368   We intervene primarily at the tower’s final block. Within each family, pooled features, fitted probes,
369
      and write vectors are therefore identical across sizes (bit-identical for Gemma 3 4B and 12B and for
      LLaVA-1.5; equal within one bf16 rounding step for Gemma 3 27B and MedGemma 27B, direction
370
      cosines above 0.9987). Readability is identical across sizes by construction. The connector and
371
      language model determine every difference in Figure 5 through how they read the same written
372   representation. These differences are large relative to every noise source in the grid (Table 14).
373   Under the identical write on the same 600 patients, Gemma 3 4B and 12B differ in 𝑂 𝑞 by −0.83
374   [−0.85, −0.81] on NIH Effusion. The difference between 12B and 27B is +0.79 [+0.76, +0.82]. In
375   11 of the 12 shared-tower pair–dataset combinations, the paired patient-bootstrap interval for Δ𝑂 𝑞
376   excludes zero for five or six of the six concepts. The median |Δ𝑂 𝑞 | is 0.6–3.7 times the families’
377   refit standard deviation (up to 8.8 times for single concepts). In 12B, competing directions own the
      chest answers outright (𝑂 Effusion = −0.83 on both chest sets, 𝑂 Mass = −0.65, 𝑂 Pneumothorax = −0.71).


