415   5.5    Size and family
416
417
      On the chest sets, ownership is concentrated in a few readers and varies by concept and dataset
      (Figure 6; Table 4). Qwen2.5-VL owns no concepts at 3B or 7B. At 32B, it owns Cardiomegaly. At
418
      72B, it owns Atelectasis (𝑂 = 0.54), Cardiomegaly, and Mass. Effusion is anti-owned at every size.
419
      Lingshu, the medical Qwen2.5-VL derivative, owns three CheXpert concepts at 7B and five at 32B,
420   the grid’s highest clinical ownership. InternVL3.5 answers every NIH question at every size. Its
421   writes remain within 0.04 of zero on the chest sets. LLaVA-1.5 reads the chest concepts but answers
422   none above chance and owns none.
423
424   5.6    Controls and alternatives
425
426   The reference family and additional controls behave as designed across the grid (Figure 2d; Table 10).
427   Owned concept writes rank 1–6 among the 120 compared effects. The concept write typically ranks
428   in the top decile on the chest sets.
429
430   Geometry, scale, saturation, refits, numerics. No measurement alternative explains the deficit
431   (Tables 11–20; Appendix A.7). The strongest competitor matches the most similar direction or the
      most co-occurring label at chance rate. Verdicts agree on the logit scale in 341 of 348 cells. COCO


