540
      Reproducibility statement
541
542
      The registered protocol file fixes the loci, projection, probe settings, dose grid, reference family,
543   templates, modules, gates, and decision rules; its identifier and code commit are recorded in every
544   block’s scorecard. The release contains the evaluation code and adapters, the protocol file, the cohort
545   manifests with their seeds, the fitted directions, the per-image outcomes of every module, every block’s
546   scorecard and coverage file, the rendered prompts, and the pinned checkpoint revisions (Table 2);
547   every table and figure in the paper is regenerated from those files by the scripts in the release.
548
549
      Ethics statement
550
551
      The study uses three public datasets under their published terms: NIH ChestX-ray14 (NIH Clinical
552
      Center), CheXpert Plus (Stanford AIMI, accessed through its data-use agreement), and COCO
553
      (annotations CC BY 4.0). All radiographs are de-identified by their providers; no protected health
554   information was accessed, and no image or report is redistributed. The write test evaluates model
555   behaviour under activation edits and is not a diagnostic tool; its grades describe what a probe direction
556   does inside a model and carry no claim of clinical benefit.
557
