648
      A     Campaign details
649
650
      This appendix lists the checkpoints and their consumed loci, the acceptance decisions, the coverage of
651
      the campaign, and the per-concept results of every completed block.
652
653
      A.1   Labels, registration, and artifact
654
655
      Labels. Concept labels are the report-derived labels shipped with each dataset (NIH ChestX-
656   ray14 finding labels; the CheXpert labeler output distributed with CheXpert Plus; COCO instance
657   annotations). A row is positive for label 1, negative for label 0, and unknown when the labeler returns
658   uncertain or blank. We exclude unknown rows from probe fitting, selectivity, and answer AUROC.
659   We write and score them like every other row. Cohorts are fixed manifests drawn with recorded seeds.
660   Training and test cohorts are patient-disjoint. All cohorts are disjoint from every seed-study cohort.
661   Table 5 gives per-concept counts.
662
663   Registration. The protocol was frozen before any grid block was scored. The loci, projection and
664   probe settings, dose, reference family, six templates, module set, seven gates, and three decision
665   rules are those of the registered protocol file and its code commit. The seed study’s crossover and
666   confirmation analyses were registered before they were run (Appendix B). One analysis pass over the
667
      packaged outcomes produces everything reported per block. The leaderboard, write-flow share, and
      per-image examples are descriptive summaries of these outputs, added after the grid was complete.
668
669
670
      Artifact. The release contains evaluation code and adapters, the registered protocol file, cohort
      manifests with their seeds, fitted directions, per-image outcomes for every module (write, dose, refit,
671
      locus, and template rows), every block’s scorecard and coverage file, and rendered prompts. Adding a
672
      new checkpoint requires one adapter that names the block it consumes and passes the gates.
673
674
