730   A.3      Acceptance decisions
731
732   All 58 completed blocks pass checks (A), (B), (C), and (G) with zero determinism error, zero
733   change at 𝛼 = 0, and fp32-versus-model logit differences below 0.13. In check (D), the Qwen3-VL,
734   Gemma 3, MedGemma, InternVL, and Llama families exceed the 0.25-logit tolerance (up to 1.84
735   logits for Gemma 3 12B). We record these as declared deviations and neutralise them through fixed
736   batch composition. Check (E) fails for the A/B templates for LLaVA-1.5-7B and LLaVA-Med,
737
      the B-mapped templates for Qwen2.5-VL-3B and LLaVA-1.5-13B, and the yes/no and A-mapped
      templates for Llama 3.2 Vision 11B on all datasets. We record the affected cells as ineligible. Two
738
      checkpoints answer “yes” to nearly every chest question (Gemma 3 4B: clean 𝑃(yes) > 0.99 on
739
      94–97% of rows). The answerability grade records this behaviour. Three checkpoints (LLaVA-1.5
740   7B/13B, LLaVA-Med) answer at chance.
741
742
      A.4      Coverage and cost
743
744   Nineteen checkpoints are complete on all three datasets with every module (Table 6): the write matrix,
745   calibration, the five additional templates, the dose sweep, the two refits, and the connector locus on
746   NIH and COCO; the write matrix and calibration on CheXpert. Llama 3.2 Vision 11B is complete
747   with its yes/no modules ineligible. Qwen2.5-VL-72B is complete on NIH. The 72B COCO/CheXpert
748   blocks and Llama 3.2 Vision 90B were not run (compute budget). InternVL3.5-38B is complete on
749   all three datasets. The campaign consumed about 3,000 A100-hours; a chest block of a 7B checkpoint
750
      takes about ten GPU-hours.
751
