      A.7        Robustness of the deficit
938
      Every alternative direction is a vector 𝒖 in the projected, train-scaled space. We lift it to the consumed
939   space exactly as the logistic normal, by normalising ŵ = 𝑅(𝒖 ⊘ max(𝒔, 10−8 )) (Equation 2). Here
940   𝑥 = 𝑅 ⊤ h, where 𝑅 is a fixed Gaussian matrix with near-orthonormal columns. A displacement 𝑅𝜹
941   of the consumed representation therefore produces the displacement 𝑅 ⊤ 𝑅𝜹 ≈ 𝜹 of the projected
942   features. The same lift carries classifier normals, class-mean displacements, and patterns alike. We
943   compute the difference-of-means and pattern vectors in the projected space and lift them once. The
944   token-weighted variants scale the per-token dose 𝛼∥h𝑖𝑡 ∥ by a weight 𝑤 𝑡 with mean one over the
945   consumed tokens. The softmax variant preserves the L1 dose of the uniform write. The top-quarter
946   variant (𝑤 𝑡 = 4 on the 25% highest-scoring tokens) has twice the uniform write’s Frobenius norm.
947
948   Direction and label geometry. Neither correlations among the six directions nor co-occurrence of
949
      the six report labels explains why a competing direction wins (Table 11). On NIH, the six directions
      are as orthogonal as random vectors (mean off-diagonal cosine 0.019 against 0.023 for random pairs).
950
      The labels are nearly uncorrelated (mean 𝜙 = 0.026). Yet NIH shows the same off-diagonal dominance
951
      as CheXpert, where directions and labels are correlated (mean cosine 0.24; Effusion–Consolidation
952   0.51, 𝜙 = 0.74). The own direction wins in 26% of NIH and 29% of CheXpert cells. The strongest
953   competitor matches the most similar direction at chance rate (19–24%) and the most co-occurring
954   label at chance rate (17–25%). Across the 1,170 off-diagonal chest cells, the competitor’s advantage
955   𝑊𝑞,𝑑 − 𝑊𝑞,𝑞 is uncorrelated with cosine (Spearman 0.04, 𝑝 = 0.13) and with 𝜙 (0.003). Removing
956   each cell’s strongest competitor does not restore ownership: 128 of 234 chest cells (55%) have at least
957   two competitors above the own write. The natural-image families with the highest co-occurrence
958   (person with bicycle, 𝜙 = 0.14; person with dog; chair with bottle) retain ownership in 97–100% of
959   cells when competitors are restricted to those families. Of the five directions in the seed cell, Nodule
960
      is the least similar to Effusion (cosine −0.06). It still moves the Effusion answer more than Effusion’s
      own direction (0.262 against 0.190). The most similar direction, Atelectasis (cosine 0.49), moves it
961
      by 0.083.
962
963
      Scale, saturation, refits, and numerics. The grades hold on the logit scale. Ownership recomputed
964
      from the margin ℓyes − ℓno agrees with the probability-scale verdict in 341 of 348 cells. Every owned
965   cell retains 𝑂 𝑞𝑚 > 0, and 126 of 129 retain the full verdict under the same rules (Table 12). Saturation
966   counters a ceiling explanation: COCO blocks have far more rows at 𝑃(yes) > 0.99 or < 0.01 than
967   chest blocks (median block share 0.82 against 0.18 and 0.15). Restricting each cell to its unsaturated
968   rows preserves 𝑂 𝑞 > 0 in all 29 owned chest cells and in 32 of the 195 others. The same pattern holds
969   in the clean-No, clean-Yes, label-present, and label-absent strata. Refitting the probes on resampled
970   training patients changes 𝑂 𝑞 by a median of 0.03. The bf16 batch effects declared at the gates
971   (candidate-logit differences of 0.07–1.84) leave the verdicts unchanged. The margin sign agrees in
      55 of 61 blocks; the 6 disagreeing blocks contain no owned cell. Re-scoring the clean baseline in a


                                                                                      18
