1053   A.8     Write structure across the grid
1054
1055   Figure 7 summarises the 6 × 6 write matrices of every completed checkpoint. The top row shows
1056   the cell-wise median matrix for each dataset. The bottom row traces each written direction on the
1057   left to the questions it moves on the right. Band width is proportional to the mean positive answer
1058
       change across checkpoints. Bands reaching the writer’s own question are coloured; bands reaching
       other questions are grey. The share of the write reaching its own question is 24% on NIH and 22% on
1059
       CheXpert against 79% on COCO. On the chest sets, the largest sinks are the Cardiomegaly question
1060
       on NIH and the Edema and Effusion questions on CheXpert. These questions receive writes from
1061   every direction.
