1220
1221   Models and consumed loci. For LLaVA-1.5-7B (Liu et al., 2024) and Qwen2.5-VL-7B (Bai et al.,
1222   2025), we use the final visual block consumed by the connector or merger. Writing 𝛼 for the signed
1223   intervention dose, synthetic hook tests establish downstream-path membership, a bitwise 𝛼 = 0 no-op,
1224   and changed downstream representations and logits at nonzero dose. Probe and intervention therefore
1225
       share one consumed representation.
1226
1227   Controlled decodability. For image 𝑖, let h𝑖𝑡 ∈ R𝐷 denote the 𝐷-dimensional representation of
1228   visual token 𝑡 at the consumed final block; mean pooling over tokens yields h𝑖 . A fixed seed-0
1229   Gaussian matrix 𝑅 ∈ R𝐷×512 projects every model to a common readout dimension; featurewise
1230   scale 𝒔 is fitted on training rows only. We then fit logistic regression with 𝐶 = 1, maximum 2,000
1231
       iterations, and seed 0. Each of 20 control seeds maps the recurring input type (AP view indicator, sex
       indicator, and age decade, giving 39 strata) to a random label. Let 𝑦 be the real test labels and 𝑟 the
1232
       fitted probe’s continuous scores. For control seed 𝑘 ∈ {0, . . . , 19}, 𝑦 ctrl
                                                                                 𝑘 denotes the random labels
1233
       and 𝑟 𝑘ctrl the corresponding control probe scores. Selectivity compares their AUROCs:
