1533   The clinical advantage reproduces under both show coded prompts, but the Mass effects remain below
1534   the maxima of 119 random directions, with reference ranks of 3/120. These 119 directions form a
1535   fixed reference family: each rank places Mass third among the 120 compared effects. This finite
1536   descriptive ranking is not a 𝑝-value, and failure to exceed this family’s maximum does not establish
1537   nonspecificity across arbitrary direction distributions or reference-family sizes. Under is, both clinical
1538   margins are negative. Neither the cross-wording nor original-wording specificity conjunction is met.
1539   Explicit show yes/no also has a positive clinical margin, 0.2369; its paired differences from A-present
1540   and B-present span zero. Within each response instruction, changing show to is reduces the clinical
1541   margin. These paired wording contrasts are descriptive. They support wording-conditioned clinical
1542   competition, rather than an advantage attributable to answer letters alone. Mass steering increases
1543   Brier error in every cell, while all AUROC-change intervals span zero.
