       D     Prompts, Scores, and Notation
1547
       D.1   A common question and answer endpoint
1548
1549
       At the first answer position, let ℓyes and ℓno denote the maximum log probabilities among the valid single-
1550   token case and leading-space variants of each answer. The registered score is 𝑃(yes) = 𝜎(ℓyes − ℓno ),
1551   where 𝜎 is the logistic sigmoid. The original Edema cell uses “pulmonary edema,” and the closure
1552   experiment uses “consolidation” in the same template. Taking the best valid token variant for each
1553   answer makes the endpoint insensitive to which listed capitalization or leading-space form receives
1554   the highest score. This endpoint measures the relative support for yes versus no at the first answer
1555   position; it does not measure the accuracy of a generated clinical report.
1556   The shared interface makes the question–direction grid interpretable: changing a clinical direction
1557   does not change the question being scored. Differences across rows reflect different clinical questions
1558   (questions are rows of 𝑊, directions are columns), so the ownership test compares directions within
1559   each row before drawing a conclusion about the named concept.
1560
1561   D.2   Reading the intervention notation
1562
1563   Table 26 collects the notation introduced in the article. The distinction between question 𝑞 and
1564   direction 𝑑 is central: a large 𝑊𝑞,𝑑 shows that a direction moves an answer, while 𝑂 𝑞 asks whether
1565   the direction bearing that answer’s clinical name moves it more than its competitors. A positive
       ownership margin alone is not the full confirmation rule; the uncertainty and non-semantic control


                                                          29
       Under review as a conference paper at ICLR 2027




1566
       comparisons must also pass. Keeping these roles separate allows the following analyses to distinguish
1567   readability, intervention strength, and semantic attribution.
1568
1569
                                      Table 26: Notation used in the manuscript.
1570
1571    Symbol     Definition
1572    𝑞, 𝑑, 𝑐    Clinical question, steering direction, and probe concept, respectively.
1573    h𝑖𝑡        Consumed visual representation for image 𝑖 and visual token 𝑡.
1574
        𝑅, 𝒔       Fixed Gaussian projection and train-fitted featurewise scale.
        ŵ𝑐        Unit probe-normal direction for concept 𝑐 after lifting to the consumed representation.
1575
        𝛼          Signed intervention dose; |𝛼| is the perturbation norm relative to each token norm.
1576    𝑊𝑞,𝑑       Paired mean change in question 𝑞’s 𝑃(yes) under direction 𝑑.
